# What this module needs on the machine, name | kind | locator | policy | consumer | reason.
# The format and the kinds are documented in the repository root CLAUDE.md. This file names
# tools and never how to install one, since that mapping is DEPENDENCIES.map one layer up.
# Written by hand, because this module has no sub units to fold declarations from.
lf    | path | lf   | required | lf         | the file manager this entire module configures
tmux  | path | tmux | required | lfrc       | every preview, confirm, and picker here opens as a tmux popup
fzf   | path | fzf  | required | fzf-find.sh | the find and tag pickers
fd    | path | fd   | required | fzf-find.sh | listing candidates for the find picker
bat   | path | bat  | optional | lfrc       | the paged file preview bound to i
nvim  | path | nvim | optional | lfrc       | the edit popup bound to o
trash | path | trash | optional | lfrc      | moving selections to the trash rather than deleting them
git   | path | git  | optional | lfrc       | repository aware actions

# Two that ship with macOS at fixed absolute paths, which is what the system kind is for. They
# were run by these scripts long before anything declared them, and nothing noticed because the
# reconciler's undeclared tool check reads Lua and is blind to shell.
tput  | system | /usr/bin/tput | required | copy-menu.sh, tag-clear-confirm.sh, trash-confirm.sh | drawing the confirm and menu overlays, every cursor move and the hiding and showing of it
file  | system | /usr/bin/file | required | preview.sh | reading a file's mime type, which is what the preview dispatches on
